        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(doctor): bound legacy session store read with size cap",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`readLegacySessionRecords` in `src/commands/doctor-session-sqlite.ts` reads legacy session store SQLite files with `fs.readFileSync` and no size limit. A corrupted or maliciously large store file would OOM the doctor process.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nA function reading arbitrary file paths from session store targets should not allocate unbounded memory. Doctor processes run during user-initiated diagnosis — the last place a user expects an OOM crash.\n\n## What Changed\n\nAdded a `statSync` pre-check with a 50 MiB size cap before each store file read. When `statSync` returns `undefined` (file not found) and `allowMissingStore` is true, the code now checks whether the parent path is a directory to correctly distinguish ENOENT from ENOTDIR (parent path is a file), which previously caused a crash.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**All 70 tests pass (68 passed + 2 skipped):**\n\n```\n[test] queued behind the local heavy-check lock held by test, pid 1082097, cwd /home/0668000387/openclawCxbAsDev...\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.commands.config.ts\n\n RUN  v4.1.10 /home/0668000387/openclawCxbAsDev/.worktrees/pr-batch\n\n ✓ |commands| src/commands/doctor-session-sqlite.test.ts (70 tests | 2 skipped) 10879ms\n     ✓ migrates a dormant historical agent database before all-agent import compaction  333ms\n     ✓ compacts migrated agent SQLite databases and reports reclaimed pages  564ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  68 passed | 2 skipped (70)\n   Start at  10:03:54\n   Duration  24.71s (transform 10.91s, setup 1.20s, import 12.32s, tests 10.88s, environment 0ms)\n\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 37.73s\n```\n\n50 MiB is above any legitimate session store file — typical stores are under 1 MiB. The cap prevents OOM on corrupted or malformed inputs while keeping normal operation unchanged.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added `statSync` pre-check with 50 MiB size cap in `readLegacySessionRecords`\n- Added parent-directory validation for `allowMissingStore === true` to distinguish ENOTDIR from ENOENT\n- Tests cover: normal read, oversized rejection, missing store, non-directory parent path",
